    "result_text": "Full suite green: **64 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**. The change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nRedesigned the owner identity key and the duplicate/soft-match rules around it.\n\n**New identity key** \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (`model/Owner.java`) now returns the 64-char lowercase hex SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`. Added a shared static `Owner.identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` so the create pipeline computes the request's key exactly as a stored owner reports it, and a new `model/Soundex.java` (standard American Soundex) for the phonetic component.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409)** \u2014 `EnsureUniqueIdentity` now rejects solely on this single key: it hashes the request identity, iterates stored owners (skipping soft-deleted), and 409s on a whole-key match. The disposable-email-domain blocklist still runs first (unchanged pipeline order). I **removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block** driven by the computed `householdId`, and dropped the now-unused `HouseholdId` parameter and `sharesHousehold` bypass from that step.\n\n**Soft match** \u2014 `DetectPossibleDuplicate` now flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (lowest matching id) when a non-deleted existing owner has the same `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` but a **different identityKey**. Since telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones are no longer a hard duplicate \u2014 they land here as a soft match.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated the OpenAPI `identityKey` description/example and the `DuplicateIdentityException` / `DeriveHouseholdId` javadocs to reflect the new key. `householdId` is still computed and stamped (for household size, region, etc.); it just no longer participates in duplicate detection.\n\nVerified: the targeted identity/household/soft-match tests (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp13, Cp25, Cp28, Cp35, Cp36, Cp46, Cp52) and the full suite of 64 tests all pass.",
